WEBVTT

1
00:01:13.208 --> 00:01:17.375


2
00:01:17.375 --> 00:01:18.750
<b> In the previous few verses, Arjuna </b>

3
00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:25.708
<b>was talking about the sin of killing his loved ones</b>
<b>and his close relatives in the war. </b>

4
00:01:25.708 --> 00:01:26.666
<b>And now,</b>

5
00:01:26.666 --> 00:01:31.458
<b>he is analyzing the far-reaching</b>
<b>consequences of this.</b>

6
00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:36.458
<b>He is saying that the result of</b>
<b>all this will not only be personal sin</b>

7
00:01:36.458 --> 00:01:37.250
<b>but also</b>

8
00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:40.041
<b>the downfall of an entire clan,</b>

9
00:01:40.041 --> 00:01:41.458
<b>and because of this,</b>

10
00:01:41.458 --> 00:01:47.166
<b>the moral and religious degradation</b>
<b>of countless generations to come. </b>

11
00:01:47.166 --> 00:01:50.875
<b>In these verses, he calls it</b>
<b>"kula-kshaya-krta-dosham,"</b>

12
00:01:50.875 --> 00:01:55.666
<b>meaning the grave mistake of</b>
<b>destroying one's own clan.</b>

13
00:01:56.208 --> 00:02:00.375


14
00:02:00.375 --> 00:02:04.666
<b>A clan is like a beautiful garland of pearls.</b>

15
00:02:04.666 --> 00:02:07.416
<b>The thread of tradition and culture</b>

16
00:02:07.416 --> 00:02:13.583
<b>is what strings all the family members</b>
<b>together like pearls.</b>

17
00:02:13.583 --> 00:02:16.291
<b>If this thread of tradition breaks,</b>

18
00:02:16.291 --> 00:02:18.041
<b>the garland will scatter.</b>

19
00:02:18.041 --> 00:02:21.750
<b>Where this beautiful garland once</b>
<b>adorned someone's neck,</b>

20
00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:26.416
<b>now those very pearls will lie</b>
<b>scattered on the ground,</b>

21
00:02:26.416 --> 00:02:30.208
<b>rolling here and there aimlessly. </b>

22
00:02:30.208 --> 00:02:32.500
<b>Such will be the result of this war. </b>

23
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.916
<b>Where the elders of the family will not survive.</b>

24
00:02:35.916 --> 00:02:40.500
<b>It is the elders who keep the thread</b>
<b>of tradition strong.</b>

25
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:44.833
<b>We are the ones who pass on the values</b>
<b>to the coming generations.</b>

26
00:02:44.833 --> 00:02:46.375
<b>If they do not survive,</b>

27
00:02:46.375 --> 00:02:47.958
<b>this chain will break,</b>

28
00:02:47.958 --> 00:02:51.458
<b>and sin will find a home in this very gap.</b>

29
00:02:51.458 --> 00:02:53.166
<b>If good values do not remain,</b>

30
00:02:53.166 --> 00:02:56.333
<b>children will only learn bad things.</b>

31
00:02:56.333 --> 00:03:01.750
<b>Slowly, the vine of unrighteousness will</b>
<b>start spreading and will engulf everyone, </b>

32
00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:05.041
<b>whether they are the boys or girls of the house,</b>

33
00:03:05.041 --> 00:03:07.375
<b>men or women.</b>

34
00:03:07.375 --> 00:03:10.708
<b>From unrighteousness,</b>
<b>unrighteous offspring will be born.</b>

35
00:03:10.708 --> 00:03:14.750
<b>And such generations, who have</b>
<b>already forgotten respect and honor, </b>

36
00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.833
<b>why will they perform the</b>
<b>shraddha of their ancestors?</b>

37
00:03:17.833 --> 00:03:21.666
<b>The souls of the ancestors will also</b>
<b>be distressed and sorrowful.</b>

38
00:03:21.666 --> 00:03:24.125
<b>The living will be sorrowful,</b>
<b>the dead will also be sorrowful,</b>

39
00:03:24.125 --> 00:03:27.916
<b>such a family will spread not</b>
<b>happiness and peace in society,</b>

40
00:03:27.916 --> 00:03:32.708
<b>but only chaos and unrest.</b>

41
00:03:32.708 --> 00:03:34.291
<b>From Arjuna's perspective,</b>

42
00:03:34.291 --> 00:03:38.291
<b>This war will affect not only</b>
<b>individuals but also families,</b>

43
00:03:38.291 --> 00:03:48.291
<b>future generations, the living, the dead,</b>
<b>and the world itself with sorrow.</b>

44
00:03:48.291 --> 00:03:52.166
<b>Here Arjuna addresses</b>
<b>Shri Krishna as Varshneya.</b>

45
00:03:52.166 --> 00:03:55.791
<b>Varshneya means a</b>
<b>descendant of the Vrishni clan. </b>

46
00:03:55.791 --> 00:03:58.541
<b>It is as if Arjuna is reproaching,</b>

47
00:03:58.541 --> 00:04:00.416
<b>"O descendant of the Vrishni clan,</b>

48
00:04:00.416 --> 00:04:05.250
<b>you too would want your</b>
<b>clan not to be destroyed?</b>

49
00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.625
<b>I too am desiring the same thing."</b>

50
00:04:08.291 --> 00:04:12.458


51
00:04:12.458 --> 00:04:15.083
<b>You are listening to the Gita,</b>

52
00:04:15.083 --> 00:04:16.791
<b>reading it,</b>

53
00:04:16.791 --> 00:04:23.041
<b>to give the right direction to</b>
<b>your mind and intellect, aren't you? </b>

54
00:04:23.041 --> 00:04:24.625
<b>This means</b>

55
00:04:24.625 --> 00:04:28.875
<b>that you well understand the</b>
<b>importance of proper guidance.</b>

56
00:04:28.875 --> 00:04:35.125
<b>And the right path can only be shown</b>
<b>by the one who has walked that path, </b>

57
00:04:35.125 --> 00:04:36.583
<b>who has experienced</b>

58
00:04:36.583 --> 00:04:38.750
<b>every right turn</b>

59
00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:43.083
<b>and also every wrong turn</b>
<b>where there are pitfalls.</b>

60
00:04:43.083 --> 00:04:45.291
<b>You tell me,</b>

61
00:04:45.291 --> 00:04:47.333
<b>What would be appropriate?</b>

62
00:04:47.333 --> 00:04:51.208
<b>To repeat the mistakes made by others?</b>

63
00:04:51.208 --> 00:04:57.291
<b>Or to learn from their experiences?</b>

64
00:04:57.291 --> 00:04:59.291
<b>On the path of life,</b>

65
00:04:59.291 --> 00:05:03.291
<b>it is essential to learn from one's elders.</b>

66
00:05:03.291 --> 00:05:08.166
<b>The crossroads where you</b>
<b>may be standing today in some dilemma,</b>

67
00:05:08.166 --> 00:05:13.250
<b>they have passed through that</b>
<b>same crossroads many times.</b>

68
00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:16.125
<b>Think about it.</b>

69
00:05:16.125 --> 00:05:18.916
<b>Understand the importance of your elders.</b>

70
00:05:19.458 --> 00:05:23.666


71
00:05:23.666 --> 00:05:27.166
<b>Regular exercise is a kind of ritual.</b>

72
00:05:27.166 --> 00:05:28.333
<b>Similarly,</b>

73
00:05:28.333 --> 00:05:34.250
<b>meditating for a few moments</b>
<b>every day is also a ritual.</b>

74
00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:38.583
<b>You cleanse your body by bathing every day.</b>

75
00:05:38.583 --> 00:05:40.833
<b>That too is a ritual.</b>

76
00:05:40.833 --> 00:05:41.708
<b>Daily, </b>

77
00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:46.541
<b>repetitive actions are personal rituals.</b>

78
00:05:46.541 --> 00:05:49.625
<b>Some for peace of mind,</b>

79
00:05:49.625 --> 00:05:53.083
<b>some for keeping the body healthy.</b>

80
00:05:53.083 --> 00:05:54.708
<b>In the same way,</b>

81
00:05:54.708 --> 00:05:58.166
<b>rituals are necessary for every family.</b>

82
00:05:58.166 --> 00:06:00.500
<b>Traditions are necessary.</b>

83
00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:05.250
<b>Don't consider these as hollow religious acts.</b>

84
00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:06.041
<b>religion,</b>

85
00:06:06.041 --> 00:06:06.958
<b> goodness,</b>

86
00:06:06.958 --> 00:06:11.916
<b>and culture are maintained by traditions. </b>

87
00:06:11.916 --> 00:06:15.625
<b>Traditions keep family members united.</b>

88
00:06:15.625 --> 00:06:20.416
<b>Traditions increase harmony</b>
<b>and affection among them.</b>

89
00:06:20.416 --> 00:06:25.791
<b>Traditions remind us of forgotten knowledge.</b>

90
00:06:25.791 --> 00:06:30.000
<b>And the responsibility for</b>
<b>these traditions falls on you.</b>

91
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.708
<b>Yes.</b>

92
00:06:31.708 --> 00:06:33.625
<b>On you.</b>

93
00:06:33.625 --> 00:06:37.416
<b>Even if you're not the eldest in your family,</b>

94
00:06:37.416 --> 00:06:43.208
<b>you're older than someone.</b>

95
00:06:43.208 --> 00:06:45.833
<b>Understand the traditions.</b>

96
00:06:45.833 --> 00:06:48.916
<b>Respect family rituals.</b>

97
00:06:48.916 --> 00:06:51.250
<b>Hold the hands of the younger ones</b>

98
00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:54.958
<b>and show them this path too.</b>

99
00:06:55.458 --> 00:06:59.500


100
00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:03.500
<b>What makes an organization</b>
<b>different from others? </b>

101
00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:07.041
<b>People come and go,</b>

102
00:07:07.041 --> 00:07:07.791
<b>but</b>

103
00:07:07.791 --> 00:07:12.041
<b>we often say that this</b>
<b>organization is good, this one isn't.</b>

104
00:07:12.041 --> 00:07:15.416
<b>This one has these qualities,</b>
<b>that one has those flaws.</b>

105
00:07:15.416 --> 00:07:18.833
<b>It will be good to work here, not there.</b>

106
00:07:18.833 --> 00:07:21.875
<b>Every organization has its own nature,</b>

107
00:07:21.875 --> 00:07:24.750
<b>which takes shape slowly.</b>

108
00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:28.250
<b>And both the credit and discredit for this</b>

109
00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:33.875
<b>go to the higher officials there.</b>

110
00:07:33.875 --> 00:07:36.583
<b>For continuous progress,</b>

111
00:07:36.583 --> 00:07:40.333
<b>some values are essential in every organization.</b>

112
00:07:40.333 --> 00:07:41.833
<b>Respect for people,</b>

113
00:07:41.833 --> 00:07:43.666
<b>praise for good work, </b>

114
00:07:43.666 --> 00:07:46.458
<b>guidance on mistakes,</b>

115
00:07:46.458 --> 00:07:50.458
<b>making everyone feel the</b>
<b>importance of their work.</b>

116
00:07:50.458 --> 00:07:55.000
<b>If all these also take the</b>
<b>form of tradition and rituals,</b>

117
00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:01.250
<b>then nothing can stop</b>
<b>that organization's success. </b>

118
00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:05.875
<b>As a leader or high official, it is your responsibility</b>

119
00:08:05.875 --> 00:08:13.791
<b>to both follow these values</b>
<b>and encourage others towards them. </b>

120
00:08:13.791 --> 00:08:19.500
<b>And then, before you know it, these values</b>
<b>will become the nature of your organization.</b>

121
00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:22.166
<b>Then people will say about you,</b>

122
00:08:22.166 --> 00:08:24.833
<b>that this organization has great strength,</b>

123
00:08:24.833 --> 00:08:30.000
<b>there is great respect for people here.</b>

124
00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.208
<b>These are professional rituals.</b>

125
00:08:33.208 --> 00:08:35.750
<b>Follow them, </b>

126
00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:38.125
<b>and encourage them too.</b>

